</style></head><body id="page-top" class="utk destination-layout"><a href="#main" class="skip">Skip to content</a><div class="topline" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g><span data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>ROOTED IN ODISHA. OPEN TO THE WORLD.</span><span lang="or" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>ପ୍ରୋଜେକ୍ଟ ଓଡ଼ିଶା</span></div><header class="header wrap utk-header" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g><a class="home-link" href="/" aria-label="Project Odisha home" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g><span class="brand brand-en" lang="en"><img class="brand-signature" src="/assets/brand-v4/project-odisha-en-colour.svg" alt="Project Odisha" width="850" height="140"></span></a><nav class="utk-nav desktop-navigation" aria-label="Main navigation" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g><a href="/explore/" aria-current="page" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Explore</a><a href="/books/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Books</a><a href="/journey/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>My journey</a><a href="/about/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Our purpose</a><a class="nav-contribute utk-button utk-button--secondary" href="/contribute/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Be part of it <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>↗</span></a></nav><details class="mobile-navigation" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g><summary data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Menu</summary><nav aria-label="Main navigation" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g><a href="/explore/" aria-current="page" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Explore</a><a href="/books/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Books</a><a href="/journey/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>My journey</a><a href="/about/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Our purpose</a><a href="/contribute/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Be part of it</a></nav></details></header><script type="module">var e=document.querySelector(`.mobile-navigation`);e?.addEventListener(`keydown`,t=>{t.key===`Escape`&&e.open&&(e.open=!1,e.querySelector(`summary`)?.focus(),t.preventDefault())});</script><main id="main" tabindex="-1"><article class="article-reading preservation-story" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a class="collection-return" href="/explore/" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>← Explore Odisha</a><header data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><h1 data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Odia Bibhaba and the Work of Keeping Literature Available</h1><p class="article-byline" data-astro-cid-6jw2r4la>By Ahimanikya Satapathy</p><div class="journey-save" data-astro-cid-2dbio7xi><button type="button" class="button utk-button utk-button--secondary" data-save-journey="reading:stories/odia-literature-preservation" disabled data-astro-cid-2dbio7xi>Save to my journey +</button><span data-save-status role="status" data-astro-cid-2dbio7xi></span></div><noscript><p data-astro-cid-2dbio7xi>Enable JavaScript to save a journey, or print this page from your browser.</p></noscript></header><figure class="preservation-illustration" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><img src="/assets/odia-literature-preservation/reading-table-v1.jpg" srcset="/images/responsive/54e6b212d0dff59d-480.webp 480w, /images/responsive/77a9218b8fd75067-960.webp 960w, /images/responsive/5084ccde4da8ea5a-1440.webp 1440w" sizes="(max-width: 740px) 94vw, 740px" decoding="async" alt="Illustration of an open book on a cradle beside a laptop displaying a scanned page." width="1536" height="1024" fetchpriority="high" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb="true"><figcaption data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>From a preserved volume to a readable digital copy. Illustration. Project Odisha.</figcaption></figure><details class="research-contents" data-astro-cid-v555epqn><summary data-astro-cid-v555epqn>In this article</summary><nav aria-label="In this article" data-astro-cid-v555epqn><a href="#section-1" data-astro-cid-v555epqn>How a science project became an archive</a><a href="#section-2" data-astro-cid-v555epqn>Preserving the conversation around a work</a><a href="#section-3" data-astro-cid-v555epqn>More ways to keep Odia literature in circulation</a><a href="#section-4" data-astro-cid-v555epqn>What makes preservation useful</a><a href="#preservation-further-reading" data-astro-cid-v555epqn>Further reading</a><a href="#preservation-continue-reading" data-astro-cid-v555epqn>Continue reading</a><a href="#story-sources" data-astro-cid-v555epqn>Footnotes &amp; Sources</a></nav></details><script type="module" src="/_astro/ResearchContents.astro_astro_type_script_index_0_lang.BfC-iVaI.js"></script><div id="opening" class="preservation-section" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><p class="article-opening" data-source-ids data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>A book can survive and still be out of reach. Its title may appear in a bibliography, its author may be celebrated, and a copy may remain somewhere in a private collection. Yet a reader who wants to read the work may have no practical way to find it.</p><p data-source-ids="bibhaba-pathagara" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Odia Bibhaba’s Pathagara addresses that distance between remembering literature and being able to read it. Its entrance leads to newspapers, magazines, books, reference works and collected writings. Dictionaries and bibliographies sit alongside literary collections. This breadth matters: a language’s written life includes the tools people used to understand it, as well as the poems and stories they made with it.<sup><a id="ref-opening-1-bibhaba-pathagara" href="#note-bibhaba-pathagara" data-footnote-ref aria-label="Footnote 1: Odia Bibhaba Pathagara">1</a></sup></p></div><div id="section-1" class="preservation-section" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><h2 data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>How a science project became an archive</h2><p data-source-ids="bibhaba-srujanika-about" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>The group behind Odia Bibhaba is Srujanika. Its account traces the preservation effort to science writing in Odia: collecting articles and examining dictionaries for terminology led it to Gopal Chandra Praharaj’s <em data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Purnachandra Odia Bhasakosha</em> and to the difficulty of finding old publications.<sup><a id="ref-section-1-0-bibhaba-srujanika-about" href="#note-bibhaba-srujanika-about" data-footnote-ref aria-label="Footnote 2: Srujanika and digitisation">2</a></sup></p><p data-source-ids="bibhaba-srujanika-about" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Srujanika dates Project Rebati to 2004 and the digital <em data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Bhasakosha</em> to 2006. It describes homemade imaging equipment, open-source software and a see-through scanner for thick volumes. Before an archive becomes a website, somebody has to find a workable way of copying the book. Its later compilation of Odia periodicals from 1856 to 1950 included chronological and author indexes—tools for finding writing within the pages.<sup><a id="ref-section-1-1-bibhaba-srujanika-about" href="#note-bibhaba-srujanika-about" data-footnote-ref aria-label="Footnote 2: Srujanika and digitisation">2</a></sup></p><p data-source-ids="bibhaba-transition-2021" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>The institutional history also needs its dates. In a post dated 23 May 2021, Srujanika said its digitisation work had ended and that work had begun at SOA’s PPRACHIN using its equipment and experience. It said it would continue managing the website for the time being. This records a transition; it does not establish the present arrangement or mean that the online collection closed.<sup><a id="ref-section-1-2-bibhaba-transition-2021" href="#note-bibhaba-transition-2021" data-footnote-ref aria-label="Footnote 3: Odia Bibhaba blog">3</a></sup></p></div><div id="section-2" class="preservation-section" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><h2 data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Preserving the conversation around a work</h2><p data-source-ids="bibhaba-periodicals" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Old magazines preserve a different kind of literary history from a collected edition. An issue places writing beside other writing. Its contents, sequence and publication date can help a reader follow the discussion in which a poem, essay or story first circulated. Odia Bibhaba’s magazine introduction draws attention to the role of periodicals in debate and in the development of writers. It also describes the difficulty of locating surviving issues.<sup><a id="ref-section-2-0-bibhaba-periodicals" href="#note-bibhaba-periodicals" data-footnote-ref aria-label="Footnote 4: Odia magazines">4</a></sup></p><p data-source-ids data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>For a reader, the value lies in being able to return to particular publications. A general statement about the richness of Odia literature becomes a more useful invitation when it leads to something one can open and read.</p><p data-source-ids="bibhaba-gopal-chhotray" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>The Gopal Chhotray collection offers one such route. Its catalogue brings together plays, one-act plays, operas, collected works, translations and material labelled as unpublished manuscripts. It lists a 1974 edition of <em data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Srimati Samarjani</em>, which the collection identifies as Chhotray’s opera adaptation of Fakir Mohan Senapati’s <em data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Patent Medicine</em>. It also lists his translation <em data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Natasamrat</em> in a 1994 edition.<sup><a id="ref-section-2-2-bibhaba-gopal-chhotray" href="#note-bibhaba-gopal-chhotray" data-footnote-ref aria-label="Footnote 5: Gopal Chhotray collection">5</a></sup></p><p data-source-ids data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Together, these entries suggest questions worth pursuing in the works themselves. How does a short story change when it becomes musical theatre? What happens when a play travels into another language? A useful archive allows the reader to move beyond an author’s reputation towards the forms, editions and relationships that make up a writing life.</p></div><div id="section-3" class="preservation-section" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><h2 data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>More ways to keep Odia literature in circulation</h2><p data-source-ids data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Odia Bibhaba belongs within a wider effort to keep Odia literature available to readers and listeners. Recite World, Odia Wikisource and Odia Virtual Academy offer different ways to encounter that literature, hear its words and return to its texts.</p><p data-source-ids="recite-world-about" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><strong data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Recite World</strong> brings listening into this picture. Its own account identifies it as a programme of the Bhubaneswar-based Udaygiri Foundation Trust, intended to make Odia literary heritage accessible through listening and reading. It gives particular importance to dramatisation, pronunciation and encounters with unfamiliar words.<sup><a id="ref-section-3-1-recite-world-about" href="#note-recite-world-about" data-footnote-ref aria-label="Footnote 6: About Recite World">6</a></sup></p><p data-source-ids="recite-patent-medicine" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Its page for Fakir Mohan Senapati’s <em data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Patent Medicine</em> brings together an author introduction, a story description inviting the visitor to listen, and a PDF link.<sup><a id="ref-section-3-2-recite-patent-medicine" href="#note-recite-patent-medicine" data-footnote-ref aria-label="Footnote 7: Patent Medicine">7</a></sup> The title connects with the Gopal Chhotray adaptation catalogued by Odia Bibhaba. A reader can therefore approach the same literary work through a story presentation and the record of its transformation for the stage.</p><p data-source-ids data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>This adds another dimension to preservation: a voice can draw attention to rhythm, dialogue and humour, inviting someone to return to the written work. A recorded reading is also an interpretation. Its performer and recording deserve their own credits alongside the writer and the edition used.</p><p data-source-ids="odia-wikisource-rebati-workflow" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><strong data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Odia Wikisource</strong> shows how preservation can continue beyond the scan. Its page for Fakir Mohan Senapati’s <em data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Rebati</em> presents the story as readable Odia text, with editing history and links to reading formats. A Wikimedia account published in January 2015 describes work on <em data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Bhagabata</em> that included converting legacy-font text, proofreading and formatting. This was work on the usability and accuracy of the words, as well as their availability.<sup><a id="ref-section-3-4-odia-wikisource-rebati-workflow" href="#note-odia-wikisource-rebati-workflow" data-footnote-ref aria-label="Footnote 8: Rebati on Odia Wikisource">8</a></sup></p><p data-source-ids="odia-wikisource-barnabodha-index" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>The project also makes unfinished work visible. Its scan-linked index for the 1901 <em data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Barnabodha</em> has numbered pages and a status indicating that the file needs checking. Such signals help readers distinguish a text that is available from one whose checking is complete.<sup><a id="ref-section-3-5-odia-wikisource-barnabodha-index" href="#note-odia-wikisource-barnabodha-index" data-footnote-ref aria-label="Footnote 9: Barnabodha 1901 scan index">9</a></sup></p><p data-source-ids="ova-about-novels" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><strong data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Odia Virtual Academy</strong> provides another entrance to Odia material. Its stated remit includes books, journals, manuscripts and archival records. Its novel catalogue offers discovery by title and author and lists works such as <em data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Antima Jatra</em> and <em data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Matimatala</em>. This is useful to a reader who knows a writer’s name but needs help finding a work. A catalogue listing, however, should not be mistaken for a guarantee that every linked file is complete or searchable.<sup><a id="ref-section-3-6-ova-about-novels" href="#note-ova-about-novels" data-footnote-ref aria-label="Footnote 10: About Odia Virtual Academy">10</a></sup></p><p data-source-ids data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>These collections can overlap. A scan may travel between a digitising group, a hosting institution and a volunteer transcription project. Recognising each contribution gives a clearer account of the work than treating every website as an entirely separate rescue of the same book.</p></div><div id="section-4" class="preservation-section" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><h2 data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>What makes preservation useful</h2><p data-source-ids data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>These efforts deserve attention for the patient work they make possible: locating a copy, identifying an edition, imaging a page, recording its details, and checking its words. The finished website is the visible point at which that work reaches a reader.</p><p data-source-ids data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>For someone using an archive, a few small habits help preserve the value of what has been found. Note the author and title, but also the edition, publication year and page. Retain the link to the particular copy. If a word is unclear, keep the uncertainty visible rather than silently supplying a more familiar spelling. When quoting or republishing, look for the item’s stated reuse conditions; a download button alone does not explain them.</p><p data-source-ids data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>For families and institutions holding old publications, the first contribution may be a careful list of what survives. An incomplete run of a magazine can still be worth identifying. A title page, a missing issue, or a different edition can matter to someone trying to reconstruct a work’s history. Any digitisation should be arranged with the custodian and with appropriate care for the original.</p><p data-source-ids data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Odia Bibhaba gives us a place to begin reading. The next step is to use it attentively: open a magazine, follow an author’s collection, consult a reference work, and carry the source details into whatever we write next. Preservation becomes part of a language’s continuing life when the material can be found, examined and read again.</p></div><section id="preservation-further-reading" class="article-reading-path" aria-label="Further reading" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><h2 data-astro-cid-q224smgb="true">Further reading</h2><nav aria-label="Further reading" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><ul data-astro-cid-q224smgb><li data-astro-cid-q224smgb><a href="/stories/odia-dhaga/" class="reading-path-link" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-copy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-title" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>The Poetry We Speak <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>→</span></span></span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-q224smgb><a href="/stories/nimuhi-temple/" class="reading-path-link" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-copy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-title" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Ahimanikya and Sashisena at Nimuhi Temple <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>→</span></span></span></a></li></ul></nav></section><section id="preservation-continue-reading" class="article-reading-path" aria-label="Continue reading" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><h2 data-astro-cid-q224smgb="true">Continue reading</h2><nav aria-label="Continue reading" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><ul data-astro-cid-q224smgb><li data-astro-cid-q224smgb><a href="/stories/odia-bibhaba-visit/" class="reading-path-link has-image" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><img src="/assets/odia-bibhaba-visit/meeting-hall.jpg" srcset="/images/responsive/8601885656291e90-480.webp 480w, /images/responsive/67b489931cfc092e-960.webp 960w, /images/responsive/e6562eb9bbf0cda1-1440.webp 1440w" sizes="(max-width: 358px) calc(100vw - 2.4rem), (max-width: 600px) 320px, 180px" decoding="async" alt width="180" height="120" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb="true"><span class="reading-path-copy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-title" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>A Morning with Odia Bibhaba <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>→</span></span><span class="reading-path-description" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>My personal visit to the website relaunch at Lohia Academy, Bhubaneswar.</span></span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-q224smgb><a href="/literature/" class="reading-path-link" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-copy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-title" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Odia literature <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>→</span></span></span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-q224smgb><a href="/literature/birakishore-das/" class="reading-path-link has-image" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><img src="/images/literature/birakishore-das/reading-table-480.webp" decoding="async" alt width="180" height="120" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb="true"><span class="reading-path-copy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-title" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Birakishore Das <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>→</span></span><span class="reading-path-image-note" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Illustration: Project Odisha.</span></span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-q224smgb><a href="/stories/godabarish-mahapatra-and-niankhunta/" class="reading-path-link has-image" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><img src="/images/stories/godabarish-niankhunta-480.webp" decoding="async" alt width="180" height="120" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb="true"><span class="reading-path-copy" data-astro-cid-q224smgb><span class="reading-path-title" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Godabarish Mahapatra <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>→</span></span><span class="reading-path-image-note" data-astro-cid-q224smgb>Illustration: Project Odisha.</span></span></a></li></ul></nav></section><section id="story-sources" class="article-footnotes" aria-labelledby="footnote-title" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><h2 id="footnote-title" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Footnotes &amp; Sources</h2><ol data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><li id="note-bibhaba-pathagara" tabindex="-1" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="https://odiabibhaba.in/pathagara/" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Odia Bibhaba Pathagara</a>. Library categories and descriptions. <span class="footnote-returns" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="#ref-opening-1-bibhaba-pathagara" data-footnote-backref aria-label="Return to passage 1 for footnote 1" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>↩</a></span></li><li id="note-bibhaba-srujanika-about" tabindex="-1" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="https://odiabibhaba.in/en/about/" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Srujanika and digitisation</a>, Odia Bibhaba. Organisational account of Project Rebati, the digital <em data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Bhasakosha</em>, imaging equipment and the periodical compilation. Its undated cumulative page totals are not used here as current figures. <span class="footnote-returns" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="#ref-section-1-0-bibhaba-srujanika-about" data-footnote-backref aria-label="Return to passage 1 for footnote 2" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>↩</a><a href="#ref-section-1-1-bibhaba-srujanika-about" data-footnote-backref aria-label="Return to passage 2 for footnote 2" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>↩2</a></span></li><li id="note-bibhaba-transition-2021" tabindex="-1" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="https://odiabibhaba.in/en/blog/" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Odia Bibhaba blog</a>, entry dated 23 May 2021. Srujanika’s dated account of the transition; no completed handover or current staffing claim. <span class="footnote-returns" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="#ref-section-1-2-bibhaba-transition-2021" data-footnote-backref aria-label="Return to passage 1 for footnote 3" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>↩</a></span></li><li id="note-bibhaba-periodicals" tabindex="-1" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="https://odiabibhaba.in/patrika/" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Odia magazines</a>, Odia Bibhaba. Periodical context and surviving-copy access difficulties. <span class="footnote-returns" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="#ref-section-2-0-bibhaba-periodicals" data-footnote-backref aria-label="Return to passage 1 for footnote 4" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>↩</a></span></li><li id="note-bibhaba-gopal-chhotray" tabindex="-1" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="https://odiabibhaba.in/en/compilations/gopal-chhotray-e/" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Gopal Chhotray collection</a>, Odia Bibhaba. Dates above identify catalogue editions, not necessarily first publication. <span class="footnote-returns" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="#ref-section-2-2-bibhaba-gopal-chhotray" data-footnote-backref aria-label="Return to passage 1 for footnote 5" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>↩</a></span></li><li id="note-recite-world-about" tabindex="-1" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="https://recite.world/about-us/" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>About Recite World</a>. Programme identity and stated listening-and-reading approach. <span class="footnote-returns" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="#ref-section-3-1-recite-world-about" data-footnote-backref aria-label="Return to passage 1 for footnote 6" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>↩</a></span></li><li id="note-recite-patent-medicine" tabindex="-1" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="https://recite.world/book/patent-medicine/" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Patent Medicine</a>, Recite World. Work page and PDF link inspected; audio playback and PDF contents were not independently checked. <span class="footnote-returns" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="#ref-section-3-2-recite-patent-medicine" data-footnote-backref aria-label="Return to passage 1 for footnote 7" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>↩</a></span></li><li id="note-odia-wikisource-rebati-workflow" tabindex="-1" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="https://or.wikisource.org/wiki/ଗଳ୍ପସ୍ଵଳ୍ପ/ରେବତୀ" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Rebati on Odia Wikisource</a>, and <a href="https://diff.wikimedia.org/2015/01/14/odia-wikisource-digitizes-classic-books/" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Odia Wikisource digitizes classic books</a>, Wikimedia, 14 January 2015. The historical account describes a particular workflow; export links do not establish that every format was independently tested. <span class="footnote-returns" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="#ref-section-3-4-odia-wikisource-rebati-workflow" data-footnote-backref aria-label="Return to passage 1 for footnote 8" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>↩</a></span></li><li id="note-odia-wikisource-barnabodha-index" tabindex="-1" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="https://or.wikisource.org/wiki/ସୂଚୀ:Barnabodha_(1901).pdf" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Barnabodha 1901 scan index</a>, Odia Wikisource. Page index and checking status observed on 4 November 2026; status can change. <span class="footnote-returns" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="#ref-section-3-5-odia-wikisource-barnabodha-index" data-footnote-backref aria-label="Return to passage 1 for footnote 9" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>↩</a></span></li><li id="note-ova-about-novels" tabindex="-1" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="https://ova.gov.in/en/AboutOVA" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>About Odia Virtual Academy</a> and its <a href="https://ova.gov.in/en/Page?keyData=2RyD5qRoMIQ%3D" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>novel catalogue</a>. Collection and discovery features; no claim of complete item-level access or a completed digitisation target. <span class="footnote-returns" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="#ref-section-3-6-ova-about-novels" data-footnote-backref aria-label="Return to passage 1 for footnote 10" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>↩</a></span></li></ol></section><p class="article-update" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb><a href="/contribute/?page=%2Fstories%2Fodia-literature-preservation%2F" data-astro-cid-kxq3n2zb>Suggest an update</a>. GitHub submissions are public; omit private contact details and consent documents.</p></article></main><footer class="footer"><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div class="footer-intro"><a href="/" class="home-link" aria-label="Project Odisha home"><span class="brand brand-en" lang="en"><img class="brand-signature" src="/assets/brand-v4/project-odisha-en-colour.svg" alt="Project Odisha" width="850" height="140"></span></a><p>Discover Odisha. Imagine the possibilities.</p><p class="footer-mission">People, places and knowledge.<br>A story we build together.</p><div class="page-share" data-page-share data-astro-cid-ougg6kcf><button class="utk-button utk-button--secondary" type="button" data-share-button hidden data-astro-cid-ougg6kcf>Share this page</button><p data-share-status role="status" data-astro-cid-ougg6kcf></p><label data-share-fallback hidden data-astro-cid-ougg6kcf>Page link<input readonly type="url" aria-label="Page link to copy" data-astro-cid-ougg6kcf></label></div><script type="module" src="/_astro/PageShare.astro_astro_type_script_index_0_lang.ChO52ZaM.js"></script></div><nav class="footer-links" aria-label="About Project Odisha"><h2 class="eyebrow">The project</h2><a href="/about/">About the project</a><a href="/founder/">The founder</a><a href="/about/editorial-process/">Our editorial process</a><a href="/global-connections/">Global Connections</a></nav><nav class="footer-links" aria-label="Explore and contribute"><h2 class="eyebrow">Take part</h2><a href="/books/">Books</a><a href="/characters/">Character worlds</a><a href="/contribute/">Contribute</a><a href="/contribute/?page=%2Fstories%2Fodia-literature-preservation%2F">Suggest a correction</a></nav><nav class="footer-links" aria-label="Website help"><h2 class="eyebrow">Useful links</h2><a href="/how-to-use/">How to use Project Odisha</a><a href="/how-to-use/#privacy">Privacy</a><a href="#page-top">Back to top ↑</a></nav></div><div class="wrap footer-bottom"><span>Founded by Ahimanikya Satapathy.</span><span>Preview edition · articles await editorial review</span></div></footer><script id="analytics-config" type="application/json">{"id":"G-9WJHZGN1EM","canonical":"https://projectodisha.org/stories/odia-literature-preservation/","title":"Odia Bibhaba and the Work of Keeping Literature Available · Project Odisha","allowedPaths":["/stories/odia-literature-preservation/"]}</script><section class="analytics-choice wrap" id="analytics-choice" aria-labelledby="analytics-heading" hidden data-astro-cid-5krk3x6l><h2 id="analytics-heading" data-astro-cid-5krk3x6l>Your cookie choices</h2><p data-astro-cid-5krk3x6l>We use optional cookies to understand how our website i